---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// The Privacy page ("Build the Privacy page", docket:v1:task:01M35J0JQ47JH6V004ZFJZDXFN).
// Wording is the task's draft Specification, word for word. "Finalize the
// Privacy policy wording" (docket:v1:task:01M35J0JT1968NPPR4TBRBFSS7)
// replaces it later — the whole block between the two DRAFT NOTICE comments
// below is what to delete once that happens.

const title = 'Privacy · Week Without Driving Las Vegas';
const description = 'What Week Without Driving Las Vegas collects, why, and when it is deleted.';
const contactEmail = 'wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org';
const contactMailto = `mailto:${contactEmail}`;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="container-prose py-16 md:py-24">
    {
      /* DRAFT NOTICE — remove this block, and this comment, once
        "Finalize the Privacy policy wording" is approved. */
    }
    <div
      class="mb-10 flex items-start gap-3 border border-primary bg-primary-container px-5 py-4 text-on-primary-container"
    >
      <span class="mt-0.5 font-bold" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed">
        Draft: final wording pending review. This page holds the wording from "Build the Privacy
        page" until "Finalize the Privacy policy wording" is approved.
      </p>
    </div>
    {/* END DRAFT NOTICE */}

    <h1 class="text-display-sm">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">
      Last updated: September 22, 2026.
    </p>

    <article class="prose-doc mt-8">
      <p>
        Week Without Driving Las Vegas (lvwwd.org) is run by Las Vegans for Better Transit (LVBT), a
        volunteer nonprofit in Las Vegas. This page explains what information we collect, why, who
        helps us handle it, and when we delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You can pledge, play bingo and read every guide without giving us your name, email address
          or phone number.
        </li>
        <li>
          Everything personal we collect is optional, and we use it only for Week Without Driving
          2026.
        </li>
        <li>
          We delete personal campaign information on November 30, 2026. You can ask us to delete
          yours sooner.
        </li>
        <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
        <li>
          LVBT's newsletter is separate. If you choose to join it, it keeps your email address until
          you unsubscribe.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
      <p>We collect these kinds of personal information, and only when you give them to us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Phone number</li>
        <li>Instagram handle</li>
        <li>Screenshots and photos you upload</li>
        <li>
          Whether you're 13 to 17 and your parent or guardian agrees to the giveaway's Official
          Rules
        </li>
        <li>A notification address from your browser, if you turn on notifications</li>
        <li>Your reply, if you win the giveaway and answer our text message</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Your pledge. When you pledge, we store the level you chose (One Trip, One Day or One Week).
        If you came from a partner organization's link or QR code, we also store that organization's
        short name, so we can tell them how many people they brought. Neither of these says who you
        are.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your email address, if you give it with your pledge. If you tick "Email me a copy of my
        participant kit", we use your address to send you that one email, and we note whether it was
        sent. It is the only email lvwwd.org sends. If you also tick "Also send me LVBT's
        newsletter", we pass your address to LVBT's newsletter. See "LVBT's newsletter" below.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your giveaway entries, if you enter the giveaway. For each entry we store one way to tell
        your entries apart and to reach you if you win: your Instagram handle, or the email address
        or phone number you type on the free entry form. If you upload a screenshot or photo, we
        store it. We never publish it. If you tag @lasvegasfortransit on Instagram, a volunteer
        records your handle. If you're 13 to 17, we store that your parent or guardian agrees to the
        Official Rules. When we draw a winner, we keep a record of the draw with the winner's
        handle, email address or phone number. We contact the winner the same way they entered: by
        Instagram message, by email from{' '}
        <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a>, or by text
        message. If the winner answers our text, we keep the reply with the record of the draw.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your phone number, if you sign up for text reminders. We store your number, when you agreed,
        and whether you confirmed, so we can send you one reminder a day during the week. See "Text
        messages" below.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your notification address, if you turn on notifications. Your browser gives us an address
        that lets us send notifications to that one browser. It doesn't include your name or phone
        number.
      </p>

      <h2>What the site keeps on your device</h2>
      <p>Some things are saved only in your browser, on your phone or computer:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Two pledge cookies, so the site remembers your pledge. <code>lvwwd_pledge</code> holds a random
          code for your pledge, and <code>lvwwd_tier</code> holds the level you chose. They last one year,
          or until you tap "Start a new pledge" or clear your browser's data.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your bingo card: which squares you marked, and whether you chose the grid or the list.
          This is never sent to us.
        </li>
        <li>
          Whether you've already seen or closed the suggestion to add lvwwd.org to your home screen,
          so we don't keep showing it.
        </li>
        <li>
          While a browser tab is open, that tab keeps the email address you typed, whether you asked
          for the newsletter, and the short name of the partner whose link you used. They're erased
          when you close the tab.
        </li>
        <li>
          Copies of pages you've visited, such as the guides, Go, Bingo and your participant kit, so
          they work without a connection. Your browser keeps them until you clear your browser's
          data.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you turn on notifications, your browser keeps the subscription that lets us reach it.
          Tap "Stop reminders" on your participant kit to remove it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we measure use</h2>
      <p>
        We count page visits and actions like pledging with Cloudflare Web Analytics and LVBT's own
        analytics. These counts contain no personal information: no names, email addresses, phone
        numbers or IP addresses. We don't let advertisers or other companies track what you do on
        lvwwd.org across other websites.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        Only the LVBT volunteers who run the campaign can see what we collect, on a page that needs
        a sign-in. These companies help us run the site, and they use your information only to do
        that job for us:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Cloudflare hosts the site, stores the database and uploaded files, checks that forms are
          filled in by people and not bots, and provides Cloudflare Web Analytics.
        </li>
        <li>Resend sends the kit email.</li>
        <li>Beehiiv runs LVBT's newsletter, only if you ask to join it.</li>
        <li>Twilio sends text reminders.</li>
        <li>
          Your browser's notification service, from Apple, Google, Mozilla or Microsoft, delivers
          notifications.
        </li>
        <li>
          Instagram, only for tags you post publicly. When you tag @lasvegasfortransit, a volunteer
          sees your post on Instagram and records your handle. If you win, we message you there.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. If you'd still like to tell us not to sell it,
        email <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a> and we'll confirm.
      </p>

      <h2>Text messages</h2>
      <p>
        If you sign up for text reminders, you agree to get texts from Week Without Driving Las
        Vegas at the number you gave. We first text you to confirm. You're signed up only after you
        reply YES. Then we send 1 reminder a day, October 1 to 8, 2026, at about 8 am. Reply STOP at
        any time to stop. Reply HELP for help. Message and data rates may apply. You don't have to
        sign up for texts to take part. If you enter the giveaway with your phone number and you
        win, we text you to tell you, even if you didn't sign up for reminders. Reply CLAIM to claim
        your prize. Replying to that text never signs you up for reminders. We never share your
        phone number or your agreement to get texts with anyone for their marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        We don't knowingly collect information from children under 13. If you think a child under 13
        has given us information, email <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}
          >{contactEmail}</a
        > and we'll delete it. To enter the giveaway, you must be 13 or older. If you're 13 to 17, your
        parent or guardian must agree to the Official Rules before you enter.
      </p>

      <h2>LVBT's newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        LVBT's newsletter is separate from this campaign. If you tick "Also send me LVBT's
        newsletter" or tap "Join the newsletter", we send your email address to Beehiiv, the service
        LVBT uses for its newsletter, and Beehiiv emails you to confirm. We keep a record that you
        asked: the time, the form you used, and a scrambled code made from your address instead of
        the address itself. Because the newsletter belongs to LVBT and not to this campaign, your
        subscription and that record are not deleted on November 30, 2026. You can unsubscribe at
        any time with the link at the bottom of any newsletter email.
      </p>

      <h2>When we delete it</h2>
      <p>
        On November 30, 2026, we delete every email address, phone number, Instagram handle,
        uploaded screenshot, giveaway entry, draw record and notification address we hold for this
        campaign. After that we keep only anonymous totals: how many people pledged at each level
        and through each partner organization, and the anonymous counts of page visits and actions.
      </p>

      <h2>See, change or delete your information</h2>
      <p>
        To see the information we hold about you, correct it, or delete it before November 30, 2026,
        email <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a>. Tell us the
        email address, phone number or Instagram handle you used. We'll reply within 7 days.
      </p>
      <p>You can also stop messages yourself at any time:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Kit email: use the unsubscribe link at the bottom of the email. This also deletes your
          email address from lvwwd.org.
        </li>
        <li>Text reminders: reply STOP.</li>
        <li>
          Notifications: tap "Stop reminders" on your participant kit, or turn off notifications for
          lvwwd.org in your browser or phone settings.
        </li>
        <li>LVBT's newsletter: use the unsubscribe link in any newsletter email.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this page, we change the "Last updated" date at the top and add a short note
        under it saying what changed.
      </p>

      <h2>More</h2>
      <p>
        Read our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> and the giveaway's{' '}
        <a href="/giveaway/rules">Official Rules</a>. Questions? Email{' '}
        <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
